# jeeva/ and ocr-service/ are separate Python services deployed on Render,
# not Vercel -- but Vercel's zero-config Python detection scans the whole
# repo for requirements.txt regardless of the project's Root Directory
# setting, and was trying to build ocr-service (torch + transformers) as
# a stray serverless function, failing on Vercel's 500MB function-size cap.
#
# Leading slash matters: an unanchored "jeeva/" matches a directory named
# jeeva at ANY depth (same rule as .gitignore) -- it was also excluding
# apps/web/public/jeeva/, which holds the orb's real orb.js/mic.js static
# assets, breaking the orb on the live site. Anchor to the repo root only.
/jeeva/
/ocr-service/
